course: dictionary
lesson: 6825
title: Working out a medical word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Doctors use some special words, and you can work many of them out from the words around them. «A doctor looks inside the ear with an otoscope, a small torch with a magnifying lens.» The clues are looks inside the ear, torch and magnifying lens. So an otoscope must be a tool for looking inside something, here your ear.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense. Does «a doctor looks inside the ear with a tool for looking inside the ear» make sense? Yes, so your meaning is probably right.
explain: Some words are built from smaller parts. Oto comes from an old Greek word for ear, and scope means a tool for looking at something, as in microscope or telescope. Put them together and you get a tool for looking at the ear.
fact: An otoscope is a small medical tool with a light and a magnifying lens.
fact: A doctor uses an otoscope to look inside your ear.
fact: With an otoscope, a doctor can check the ear canal and the eardrum for wax, infection or damage.
fact: «Otoscope» is built from parts: oto means ear and scope means a tool for looking at something.
fact: Some kids' doctor play sets include a toy otoscope, so you can pretend to be the doctor.
exercise: «A doctor looks inside the ear with an otoscope, a small torch with a magnifying lens.» What is an otoscope? | A loud bell rung in hospitals | A kind of hat worn by doctors | *A small medical tool with a light and a magnifying lens for looking inside the ear | A tool for measuring how tall you are
exercise: In the same sentence, who uses an otoscope? | The ear | A magnifying glass on its own | *A doctor | A torch
exercise: Some kids' doctor play sets include a toy otoscope. What is a toy otoscope for? | Cleaning shoes | Cooking dinner | *Pretending to be a doctor and looking in a toy ear
test: The word otoscope has two parts: oto means ear and scope means a tool for looking at something. What does an otoscope help a doctor do? | *Look inside an ear | Taste food | Hear far away | Count steps
test: Which check can a doctor make with an otoscope? | Measuring your shoe size | Counting your teeth | Checking the weather | *Checking the ear canal and eardrum for wax, infection or damage
exam: Which meaning makes the sentence «A doctor looks inside the ear with an otoscope» make sense? | A type of cloud | *A medical tool for looking inside the ear | A musical instrument played with the mouth | A kind of cake
